      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T21:16:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, so I\u0027m looking at this and thinking a couple of things:\n\n1) We should probably take the chance here and instead of using `DawnProcTable`, introduce a new proc table that is `webgpu` compliant, i.e. it would try to use the upstream header instead. This would make more sense w.r.t this being a `WebGPU` backend. It would make this backend\u0027s capabilities a subset of the native\u0027s capabilities, but that should be fine?\n\n2) I\u0027m thinking that we should have a way to specify this table also. I\u0027m imagining that in Dawn, we could have a `RequestAdapterOptions` extension that allows specifying the specific table overrides we want to use here. This would make it fairly similar to the wire where we have `WireServerDescriptor` which sets the procs for the wire server. If we have the extension, it could be a way to get rid of the recursion issues you saw as well, since we could hide the WebGPU backend unless we see that extension, and remove that chain when we recurse the first time?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "c5d541ad3b6045df480039e752de909e47822ee3",
