      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T00:46:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The webgpu::PhysicalDevice requires to be backed by a \"lower layer\" implementation adapter or physical device to create the underlying apiDevice and query the features, limits, etc.\n\nWe cannot initialize such adapter inside InitializeImpl etc. as these are called inside `EnumerateAdapters` and doing so ends in an infinte recursion.\n\n[Some attempts](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/241174/) on reuse the adapter populated by `EnumerateAdapters` to init the adapterImpl after the enumerating for loop. but this breaks the frontend/backend isolation. It also has other bugs probably because adapters are abstract layer objects that are have multiple instances per physical device.\n\nAnother attempt idea is to create the \"lower layer\" physical device inside webgpu::physicalDevice by maybe duplicate some logic from instance/backendconnection (`DiscoverPhysicalDevices`). Is PhysicalDevice created once per backend on a dawn instance?\n\nWould like to hear your inputs.",
      "revId": "c5d541ad3b6045df480039e752de909e47822ee3",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "775c4a52_6855cc3d",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/PhysicalDeviceWGPU.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-10T02:34:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems to me that DiscoverPhysicalDevices should find adapters before creating PhysicalDevices. That would also allow us to make one webgpu::PhysicalDevice for each other backend.\n\nThe recursion gets complicated if we do that in `webgpu::Backend::DiscoverPhysicalDevices`, but what if we special case it in `InstanceBase::EnumeratePhysicalDevices` so that it first discovers all the non-webgpu-backend `PhysicalDevice`s, and then makes a webgpu-backend `PhysicalDevice` wrapping each one (or just the first one) and adds it to the return list?\n\nI don\u0027t know super well how PhysicalDevice works so that might require caching (so we only create one wrapper for each real PhysicalDevice).\n\nThis will require the webgpu backend to know about PhysicalDevice which isn\u0027t part of the API, but I think that\u0027s fine.\n\n(I\u0027ve reviewed everything except for the rest of this file since it seems like it might change significantly)",
      "parentUuid": "8e936b6c_06bd00ee",
      "revId": "c5d541ad3b6045df480039e752de909e47822ee3",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
