      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T13:13:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 on creating the underlying `WGPUAdapter` in `BackendWGPU` and not here. But also something looks very wrong in this file as we are using dawn::native reentrantly directly instead of going through `webgpu.h`. We should instead create a `WGPUInstance` using the procs in `BackendWGPU` (with option to use adapters for multiple device creations) and use that to enumerate a bunch of adapters. Likewise I\u0027ll wait to review the rest of this file.\n\n@Kai, the concept of an Adapter is purely frontend and backends instead list PhysicalDevices. You are right that in the WebGPU backend there should be a 1-1 relationship between `dawn::native::webgpu::PhysicalDevice` and the loopback `WGPUAdapter`.",
